WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.360
A mantle plume rises as hot solid rock

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:05.780
beneath an oceanic plate. Near the base of

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:09.400
the lithosphere, melting supplies magma that erupts through

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:13.120
fissures onto the seafloor. Repeated submarine flood basalt

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:15.720
spread across a broad area. Over millions of

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:18.500
years, those flows build an oceanic plateau above

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:21.520
the surrounding seafloor. The solid rising plume and

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:23.840
the erupted liquid basalt are different parts of

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:24.380
the process.
